    $u6221422c${"version":3,"generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:01+00:00","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","tour":{"overview":"This repository is the Python client for the Hugging Face Hub: it lets code and terminal users create repos, move files in and out, run inference, and manage Hub resources. The HfApi client is the central entry point that exposes nearly every Hub operation. It sits on the HTTP, auth and configuration core, and delegates heavy lifting to the Commit and upload pipeline and the Download and cache layer. Around them sit higher-level surfaces: HfFileSystem, buckets and hot reload, Repo cards and ModelHubMixin, the Inference client and providers, MCP and Tiny Agents, Sandbox and jobs, and Webhooks server and payloads. The hf CLI wraps most of these for humans and agents, while Code generation and quality tooling keeps the generated files and public surface consistent.","sections":[{"unit_id":"commit-upload","paragraph":"This unit turns a list of add, delete and copy operations into a single Hub commit, and decides how each file travels: as a plain payload, through LFS, or through Xet. It uses the HfApi client, the HTTP, auth and configuration core, and the Download and cache layer. It is used by the hf CLI, the HfApi client, HfFileSystem, buckets and hot reload, and the core; it tends to change together with the HfApi client, the cache layer and the core. The decision: stream the commit as newline-delimited JSON after classifying files up front, and push big folders through a streamed multi-commit pipeline on hf_xet. Git pushes, one-shot multipart commits and a separate large-folder API were passed over, because streaming allows many files per commit and Xet gives chunk-level deduplication and resumability. Lucain wrote the streaming in 2022 [human]; the Xet pipeline, which supersedes the older large-folder path, came in 2026 with Claude Code assistance [assisted]."},{"unit_id":"http-auth-config","paragraph":"This is the shared foundation for all network access: creating HTTP clients with retries and backoff, building request headers, finding and storing tokens, login flows, error types, input validation, and every environment-driven setting. It sits at the bottom of the stack, used by nearly everything else, including the hf CLI, the cache layer, inference, repo cards, filesystem and buckets, the commit pipeline, sandbox, MCP and tooling. It also lists the HfApi client and commit pipeline as things it uses, and changes alongside the HfApi client, the cache layer and the CLI. The decision: one place for retry, headers and configuration, rather than each module owning an HTTP client, so retry, error mapping and user-agent behavior stay uniform. Keyring-only auth and config files were not chosen. Celina Hanouti added multiple local tokens in 2024, and célina added browser-based OAuth login in 2026, both alone [human]. The history does not show deeper reasons."},{"unit_id":"download-cache","paragraph":"This unit downloads single files or whole repositories and keeps them in a local cache, so revisions are shared, offline use works and repeat downloads are cheap. It uses the HTTP, auth and configuration core and the HfApi client. It is used by the hf CLI, the commit pipeline, HfFileSystem, buckets and hot reload, the HfApi client, and Repo cards and ModelHubMixin, and it changes with the HfApi client, the core and the repo-card unit. The decision: a git-like cache of content-addressed blobs with snapshot links pointing at them, a fallback for systems lacking symlinks, and a metadata mode for local folders. Flat caches, git clones and an external cache service were rejected; downstream libraries rely on this layout. Julien Chaumond and Lucain designed it in 2022 [human]. Lucain and célina added the on-disk tree listing cache and a cross-repo shared blob store in 2026 with Claude Code help [assisted]."},{"unit_id":"inference","paragraph":"This unit lets users run machine-learning tasks such as chat, image generation and embeddings against Hugging Face and third-party services through one interface. It uses the HfApi client and the HTTP, auth and configuration core. It is used by the HfApi client, MCP and Tiny Agents, Code generation and quality tooling, and the hf CLI, and it changes together with the tooling, the HfApi client and the core. The decision: keep the synchronous client hand-written as the source of truth, generate the asynchronous twin from it, and give each provider a small adapter that maps the shared task interface onto that provider's HTTP API. Separate SDKs per provider and a hand-written async client were avoided, since one interface across twenty-odd providers is the goal and generation keeps sync and async in step. The history provided does not show who shaped it or when."},{"unit_id":"repocard-mixin","paragraph":"This unit reads, edits and pushes model and dataset cards, meaning the README with its metadata header, and gives machine-learning framework classes ready-made save, push and load behavior. It uses the HfApi client, the HTTP, auth and configuration core, and the Download and cache layer. It is used by the HfApi client and the hf CLI, and changes with the HfApi client, the cache layer and the tooling unit. The decision: cards are YAML front matter plus templates, and the mixin lets each framework integration share one implementation, with safetensors as the default weight format for PyTorch. Framework-specific integrations and pickle-based weights were rejected, for easier downstream adoption and for safety. Leandro von Werra, Lucain and Benjamin Muskalla made the key calls between 2022 and 2024, including the safetensors default in early 2024, all as human work [human]."},{"unit_id":"hf-filesystem-buckets","paragraph":"This unit gives Hub repos and buckets a file-system interface through fsspec, so tools like pandas and datasets can read them as if they were folders. It also holds live-following of bucket changes and hot reload for Spaces. It uses the HfApi client, the HTTP, auth and configuration core, the Download and cache layer and the Commit and upload pipeline. It is used by the hf CLI and the HfApi client, and changes with the HfApi client, the CLI and the cache layer. The decision: POSIX-like access through fsspec, with buckets as a distinct Xet-backed storage type. Offering only download and upload helpers, or inventing a custom file API, was passed over to gain interoperability with the data ecosystem. Charles wrote hot reload in February 2026 [human]; Lucain's buckets work that same month was done with Cursor [assisted]."},{"unit_id":"sandbox","paragraph":"This unit is a client for creating and talking to Hub sandboxes, with a local cache of pooled sandbox handles, alongside the types for the jobs API. It uses the HfApi client and the HTTP, auth and configuration core. It is used by the hf CLI and the HfApi client, and changes with the HfApi client, the CLI and the core. The decision: the pooled cache is tied to the context that wrote it, so a different context cannot reuse its entries, and sandbox behavior lives in a library module with the command line as a thin wrapper. Having no cache, or only remote handles, were the alternatives not taken. The history shows this was a bug fix by Lucain in September 2026, made with Claude Code [assisted]; it does not show why caching or pooling was chosen originally."},{"unit_id":"cli","paragraph":"This is the hf command line, giving terminal users, scripts and AI agents access to Hub operations with consistent output. It uses the core, the HfApi client, filesystem and buckets, the cache layer, repo cards, the commit pipeline, sandbox and inference. It is used by the tooling unit, which generates its reference docs, and by the HfApi client, and changes with the HfApi client, the core and sandbox. The decision: Typer command groups registered in one entry point, all sharing a single output object that supports auto, JSON, human, quiet and agent formats, with centralized error handling. Raw argparse or click, one script per command and plain printing were avoided for consistent machine- and human-readable output; the repository's written conventions prescribe this. célina and Lucain wrote the 2026 commands and renames [human]; later migrations and additions by célina and Caleb Fahlgren used Cursor [assisted]."},{"unit_id":"mcp-agent","paragraph":"This unit lets a language model served through the inference client call tools exposed by MCP servers. It contains a small agent loop and a command line. It uses the Inference client and providers, the HfApi client, and the HTTP, auth and configuration core. The HfApi client uses it, and it changes with the inference unit, the HfApi client, and HfFileSystem, buckets and hot reload. The decision: build the agent directly on the asynchronous inference client and the optional mcp package. Depending on external agent frameworks was avoided; the stated reason is parity with Tiny Agents in JavaScript. célina wrote it in May 2025 [human]. The history provided gives no further rationale beyond that parity goal."},{"unit_id":"webhooks","paragraph":"This unit lets a user run a small local server that receives Hub webhook events, with typed definitions of what those events contain. It is used by the HfApi client, and it changes together with the HfApi client, Repo cards and ModelHubMixin, and Code generation and quality tooling. It lists no units that it uses. The decision: an optional server built on Gradio and FastAPI, with pydantic models for the payloads. Simply documenting the raw HTTP format was not chosen; the purpose, as far as the record shows, is making webhook handling easy to set up locally and in Spaces. Lucain wrote it alone in April 2023 [human]. The history does not explain in more detail why Gradio and FastAPI were picked over other approaches."},{"unit_id":"hf-api","paragraph":"This is the main Python entry point to the Hub's REST API: repos, files, discussions, Spaces, collections, webhooks and more. It is used by the CLI, inference, tooling, repo cards, cache layer, filesystem and buckets, commit pipeline, core, sandbox and MCP, and it in turn uses most of those units. It changes with the hf CLI, the core and the cache layer. The decision: one large class, with module-level functions forwarding to its methods and a generated lazy-import package entry point, returning dataclasses. Per-resource clients, a generated OpenAPI client and pydantic responses were not chosen; the history points to backward compatibility for downstream libraries, and dataclasses replaced an older repr helper for lightweight typed results. Mario Šaško, Lucain, Freddy Boulton and Michael shaped it from 2022 to 2024 [human]; Lucain's 2026 endpoints migration was Claude Code assisted [assisted]."},{"unit_id":"codegen-quality-ci","paragraph":"This unit keeps generated files and code quality consistent: formatting, linting, type checks and the continuous-integration test suites. It uses the HfApi client, the core, the hf CLI and the inference unit, since it generates or verifies their outputs. It changes with the inference unit, the HfApi client and Repo cards and ModelHubMixin. The decision: generated outputs such as static imports, the async client, CLI reference docs and types are committed, then checked by scripts through the style and quality commands and in CI. Runtime generation and manual upkeep were not used, so the public surface and docs stay in sync. Tests are split into api, transfer and inference suites. Lucain wrote the 2022 to 2023 tooling alone [human]; his 2026 quality, test-migration and CI-split work used Claude Code [assisted]."}],"basis":"d66171de4abe","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:30:10+00:00"},"units":[{"id":"hf-api","name":"HfApi client","kind":"boundary","summary":"The monolithic HfApi class and module-level wrappers that expose nearly every Hub REST operation as the library's public API.","decision":"One giant HfApi class with a thin function-per-method facade re-exported through a statically generated lazy-import __init__, using dataclass return types.","alternatives":"Split per-resource clients (repos, spaces, collections); a generated OpenAPI client; pydantic models for responses.","why":"Backwards-compatible single entry point that downstream libraries already depend on; dataclasses replaced ReprMixin for lightweight typed results.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/hf_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/__init__.py","src/huggingface_hub/community.py","src/huggingface_hub/_space_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/_inference_endpoints.py","src/huggingface_hub/_jobs_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/endpoint_helpers.py","src/huggingface_hub/dataclasses.py"],"centrality":5,"clusters":["C1","C1.1","C1.2","C1.4"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"f590bdf","date":"2023-11-02","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Mario Šaško","subject":"Replace `ReprMixin` with dataclasses (#1788)"},{"sha":"0275ba9","date":"2022-12-08","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"Manage space hardware and secrets programmatically (#1243)"},{"sha":"aa4a792","date":"2023-07-26","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Freddy Boulton","subject":"Request Persistent Storage (#1571)"},{"sha":"ce00270","date":"2024-05-24","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Michael","subject":"[wip] Implement webhooks API (#2209)"},{"sha":"3bb08e2","date":"2026-10-01","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"Lucain","subject":"[Endpoints] Migrate catalog to the new /api/v1 API (#4928)"}],"importance":1.0,"orientation":{"purpose":"The main Python entry point for talking to the Hub's REST API: repos, files, discussions, Spaces, collections, webhooks and more. Other code and downstream libraries call it rather than making raw HTTP requests.","decision":"One large HfApi class, with module-level functions that forward to its methods and a generated lazy-import __init__. Per-resource clients, a generated OpenAPI client and pydantic responses were not chosen. The history points to backward compatibility for existing users, and dataclasses replaced ReprMixin for lightweight typed results.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/hf_api.py","what":"HfApi class and its result dataclasses"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/__init__.py","what":"public exports, auto-generated lazy imports"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_space_api.py","what":"Space runtime and hardware types"}],"shaped_by":"Several humans (Mario Šaško, Lucain, Freddy Boulton, Michael) shaped it from 2022 to 2024 [human]; Lucain's 2026 endpoints migration was [assisted].","basis":"56a4f54b5eb4","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"download-cache","name":"Download and cache layer","kind":"module","summary":"File and snapshot downloads with a git-like blob/snapshot cache, ETag resolution, Xet transfers, tree-listing cache and a cross-repo shared blob store.","decision":"Symlink-based content-addressed cache layout with degraded no-symlink fallback, local-dir metadata mode, and on-disk caching of tree listings and shared blobs.","alternatives":"Flat file cache; git clone; external cache service.","why":"Dedup of revisions and offline use; the layout is relied on by downstream libraries. Recent AI-assisted work added tree cache and shared blob store.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/file_download.py","src/huggingface_hub/_snapshot_download.py","src/huggingface_hub/_local_folder.py","src/huggingface_hub/_tree_cache.py","src/huggingface_hub/_revision.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_cache_manager.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_xet.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_xet_progress_reporting.py"],"centrality":5,"clusters":["C2","C2.1","C2.4","C2.5","C5.4"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"f124f8b","date":"2022-05-25","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Julien Chaumond","subject":"New git-aware cache file layout (#801)"},{"sha":"6a4538b","date":"2022-10-13","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"[RFC] Proposal for a way to cache files in downstream libraries (#1088)"},{"sha":"8139641","date":"2026-06-29","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"Lucain","subject":"[Download] Cache repo tree listing on disk in snapshot_download (#4394)"},{"sha":"6e3d21f","date":"2026-09-17","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"célina","subject":"[Cache] Add cross-repo shared blob store (#4498)"}],"importance":0.751,"orientation":{"purpose":"Downloads single files or whole repos from the Hub and stores them in a local cache. Revisions are deduplicated, offline use works, and repeated downloads are cheap.","decision":"A git-like cache of content-addressed blobs with snapshot symlinks, a fallback for systems without symlinks, and a metadata mode for local directories. Later work added on-disk tree-listing caching and a cross-repo shared blob store. Flat caches, git clones and external services were not used. The layout is relied on by downstream libraries.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/file_download.py","what":"hf_hub_download, ETag resolution, cache layout"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_snapshot_download.py","what":"whole-repo download"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_tree_cache.py","what":"tree listing cache"}],"shaped_by":"Julien Chaumond and Lucain designed the layout in 2022 [human]; Lucain and célina added the tree cache and shared blob store in 2026 [assisted].","basis":"786df2ad347d","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"http-auth-config","name":"HTTP, auth and configuration core","kind":"decision","summary":"Shared httpx client factory with retry/backoff, header building, token resolution and env-driven constants used by all network code.","decision":"Centralized http_backoff helpers, build_hf_headers, multi-token local store with login/OAuth/OIDC flows, and all configuration via environment-variable constants in constants.py.","alternatives":"Per-module HTTP clients; keyring-only auth; config files.","why":"Uniform retry, error mapping and user-agent behavior; multi-token support and browser OAuth were added for user convenience.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/utils/_http.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_headers.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_auth.py","src/huggingface_hub/_login.py","src/huggingface_hub/_oauth.py","src/huggingface_hub/_oidc.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_oauth_device.py","src/huggingface_hub/constants.py","src/huggingface_hub/errors.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_validators.py"],"centrality":5,"clusters":["C5","C5.3","C5.5","C5.2"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"6fcc7b3","date":"2024-10-01","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Celina Hanouti","subject":"Support multiple tokens locally (#2549)"},{"sha":"d242977","date":"2026-06-16","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"célina","subject":"[Auth] Browser-based OAuth login  (#4354)"}],"importance":0.687,"orientation":{"purpose":"The shared foundation for network access: HTTP client creation with retries, request headers, token lookup, login flows, error types and environment-driven settings.","decision":"Retry helpers, header building and every configuration constant sit in one place, instead of each module having its own HTTP client. Auth supports multiple stored tokens and browser OAuth login. Keyring-only auth and config files were not chosen. The aim is uniform retry, error and user-agent behaviour, plus convenience.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/utils/_http.py","what":"client factory and backoff helpers"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_login.py","what":"login, logout and token storage"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/constants.py","what":"environment-variable constants"}],"shaped_by":"Celina Hanouti (2024) and célina (2026) wrote the multi-token and OAuth commits alone [human].","basis":"0b4a4c7af3ac","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"commit-upload","name":"Commit and upload pipeline","kind":"flow","summary":"Turns CommitOperation objects into Hub commits, handling LFS and Xet uploads, NDJSON streaming and multi-commit upload_folder.","decision":"Commits are streamed as NDJSON with pre-upload classification into regular/LFS/Xet, and large folders are uploaded through a streamed multi-commit pipeline powered by hf_xet.","alternatives":"Git-based pushes; one-shot multipart commit; separate large-folder API.","why":"Allows many files per commit and resumable large uploads; Xet gives chunk-level dedup. The pipeline was added by AI-assisted work and supersedes upload_large_folder.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/_commit_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/lfs.py","src/huggingface_hub/_upload_pipeline.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_lfs.py","src/huggingface_hub/_commit_scheduler.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_chunk_utils.py"],"centrality":4,"clusters":["C1.3"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"7e089e6","date":"2022-10-21","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"Create commit by streaming a ndjson payload (allow lots of file in single commit) (#1117)"},{"sha":"97ea04b","date":"2026-06-16","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"Lucain","subject":"[Upload] Streamed multi-commit upload_folder powered by Xet (#4331)"}],"importance":0.524,"orientation":{"purpose":"Turns a list of add, delete and copy operations into a Hub commit. It decides how each file travels (plain, LFS or Xet) and handles large folder uploads.","decision":"Commits are sent as streamed NDJSON after files are classified as regular, LFS or Xet. Large folders go through a streamed multi-commit pipeline on hf_xet, which supersedes upload_large_folder. Git pushes, one-shot multipart commits and a separate large-folder API were not used. Xet is chosen for chunk-level dedup and resumability.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_commit_api.py","what":"CommitOperation classes and commit logic"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_upload_pipeline.py","what":"streamed multi-commit upload"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/lfs.py","what":"LFS batch upload"}],"shaped_by":"Lucain wrote the NDJSON streaming in 2022 [human] and the Xet multi-commit pipeline in 2026 [assisted].","basis":"dcab184bb304","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"cli","name":"hf CLI","kind":"boundary","summary":"Typer-based `hf` command line with groups per resource and a shared output/format layer.","decision":"Typer groups registered in hf.py, with a global `out` singleton supporting auto/json/human/quiet/agent formats, centralized error handling and generated reference docs.","alternatives":"argparse/click directly; separate scripts per command; plain print output.","why":"Consistent machine- and human-readable output (including agent use); CLAUDE.md prescribes the conventions. Much of it was built or migrated with AI assistance.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/cli","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_cli_utils.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_output.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_errors.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_help_formatter.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_framework.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/hf.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/repos.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/models.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/datasets.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/spaces.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/buckets.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/cache.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/auth.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/upload.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/download.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/jobs.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/sandbox.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/extensions.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/skills.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_skills.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_uv_script_header.py"],"centrality":4,"clusters":["C3","C3.1","C3.2","C3.3","C3.4"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"3523d1e","date":"2026-01-08","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"célina","subject":"[CLI]  Add `hf models`/`hf datasets`/`hf spaces` commands (#3669)"},{"sha":"41896bb","date":"2026-02-26","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"[CLI] Migrate to 'hf repos' instead of 'hf repo' for consistency (#3848)"},{"sha":"52503dd","date":"2026-04-10","klass":"assisted","agent":"cursor","author":"célina","subject":"[CLI] Migrate `hf cache` to `out` singleton (#4070)"},{"sha":"5ab5eec","date":"2026-03-04","klass":"assisted","agent":"cursor","author":"Caleb Fahlgren","subject":"[CLI][Datasets] - add `sql` and `parquet` commands (#3833)"}],"importance":0.682,"orientation":{"purpose":"The `hf` command-line tool. It gives terminal users, scripts and AI agents access to Hub operations with consistent output.","decision":"Typer command groups registered in hf.py, sharing one `out` output object with auto, json, human, quiet and agent formats. Errors are handled centrally and the CLI reference docs are generated. Raw argparse or click, per-command scripts and plain prints were not used. CLAUDE.md sets the conventions.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/cli/hf.py","what":"app entry point and group registration"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/cli/_output.py","what":"the `out` singleton and formats"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/cli/_cli_utils.py","what":"reusable option types and helpers"}],"shaped_by":"célina and Lucain wrote the 2026 commands and migrations [human]; later migrations and additions by célina and Caleb Fahlgren were [assisted] with Cursor.","basis":"1288e0bb0385","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"},"children":[{"id":"cli/framework","name":"CLI framework and output","kind":"module","summary":"typer_factory, shared option types, the `out` output singleton, error handling and help formatting.","decision":"A single output singleton and reusable option types that every command must use.","alternatives":"Per-command printing and options.","why":"Consistency across commands and formats.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/cli/_cli_utils.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_output.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_errors.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_help_formatter.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_framework.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/hf.py"],"centrality":5,"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"52503dd","date":"2026-04-10","klass":"assisted","agent":"cursor","author":"célina","subject":"[CLI] Migrate `hf cache` to `out` singleton (#4070)"}],"importance":0.264},{"id":"cli/resource-commands","name":"Resource commands","kind":"module","summary":"Commands for repos, models, datasets, spaces, buckets, collections, cache, auth, upload/download and webhooks.","decision":"One module per resource with verb aliases like ls/list.","alternatives":"Flat command namespace.","why":"Discoverability and consistency.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/cli/repos.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/models.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/datasets.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/spaces.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/buckets.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/cache.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/auth.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/upload.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/download.py"],"centrality":3,"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"3523d1e","date":"2026-01-08","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"célina","subject":"[CLI]  Add `hf models`/`hf datasets`/`hf spaces` commands (#3669)"},{"sha":"41896bb","date":"2026-02-26","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"[CLI] Migrate to 'hf repos' instead of 'hf repo' for consistency (#3848)"},{"sha":"5ab5eec","date":"2026-03-04","klass":"assisted","agent":"cursor","author":"Caleb Fahlgren","subject":"[CLI][Datasets] - add `sql` and `parquet` commands (#3833)"}],"importance":0.223},{"id":"cli/compute-commands","name":"Jobs, sandbox, extensions and skills","kind":"module","summary":"Commands for running jobs, sandboxes, installing CLI extensions and agent skills.","decision":"Jobs and sandbox exposed as first-class CLI groups plus an extension/skills mechanism.","alternatives":"Separate tools.","why":"unclear","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/cli/jobs.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/sandbox.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/extensions.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/skills.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_skills.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_uv_script_header.py"],"centrality":2,"scope":"architectural","history":[],"importance":0.195}]},{"id":"inference","name":"Inference client and providers","kind":"module","summary":"InferenceClient with task methods that route requests via provider adapters to HF and third-party inference services.","decision":"A sync client source of truth with a generated async twin, and per-provider adapter classes mapping the unified task API to each provider's HTTP API.","alternatives":"Separate SDK per provider; hand-written async client.","why":"Unified API across 20+ providers; codegen keeps sync/async in lockstep.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/inference/_client.py","src/huggingface_hub/inference/_common.py","src/huggingface_hub/inference/_providers","src/huggingface_hub/inference/_generated/_async_client.py","utils/generate_async_inference_client.py","src/huggingface_hub/inference/_generated/types","utils/generate_inference_types.py"],"centrality":4,"clusters":["C4","C4.1","C4.2"],"scope":"architectural","history":[],"importance":0.645,"orientation":{"purpose":"A client for running ML tasks such as chat, image generation and embeddings against Hugging Face and third-party providers through one API.","decision":"The sync InferenceClient is hand-written and the async twin is generated from it. Each provider has an adapter class mapping the shared task API to its HTTP API. Separate SDKs per provider and a hand-written async client were not chosen. Generation keeps sync and async in step.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/inference/_client.py","what":"sync InferenceClient task methods"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/inference/_providers","what":"per-provider 