n wrote the 2022–2023 tooling alone [human]; his 2026 quality, test-migration and CI-split work was [assisted].","basis":"4ac7719b8648","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"mcp-agent","name":"MCP and Tiny Agents","kind":"module","summary":"MCPClient and agent loop that connect InferenceClient to MCP tool servers, with a CLI.","decision":"Agent built on the async InferenceClient and the mcp package as an optional extra.","alternatives":"Dependence on external agent frameworks.","why":"Python parity with Tiny Agents in JS.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/inference/_mcp"],"centrality":2,"clusters":["C9"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"aee73c4","date":"2025-05-21","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"célina","subject":"[MCP] Tiny Agents in Python (#3098)"}],"importance":0.262,"orientation":{"purpose":"Lets an LLM served through InferenceClient call tools on MCP servers. It includes a small agent loop and a CLI.","decision":"The agent is built on the async InferenceClient and the optional mcp package. External agent frameworks were not used. The stated aim is parity with Tiny Agents in JS.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/inference/_mcp","what":"MCPClient, agent loop and CLI"}],"shaped_by":"célina wrote it in May 2025 [human].","basis":"2353e232d4e7","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"sandbox","name":"Sandbox and jobs","kind":"module","summary":"Client for Hub sandboxes with a pooled, context-bound cache, plus jobs API.","decision":"Pool cache bound to the context that wrote it; sandbox is a library module with CLI wrapper.","alternatives":"No caching; remote-only handles.","why":"A fix to prevent cross-context reuse; otherwise unclear.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/_sandbox.py","src/huggingface_hub/_sandbox_cache.py","src/huggingface_hub/_jobs_api.py"],"centrality":2,"clusters":["C3.3"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"40efc5e","date":"2026-09-14","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"Lucain","subject":"fix(sandbox): bind the pool cache to the context that wrote it (#4838)"}],"importance":0.262,"orientation":{"purpose":"A client for creating and talking to Hub sandboxes, with a local cache of pooled sandbox handles. Jobs API types live alongside.","decision":"The pool cache is bound to the context that wrote it, so another context cannot reuse it. Sandbox is a library module with a CLI wrapper on top. No caching and remote-only handles were not chosen. The history shows this was a fix, and other reasons are unclear.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_sandbox.py","what":"sandbox client"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_sandbox_cache.py","what":"pooled cache"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_jobs_api.py","what":"jobs API types"}],"shaped_by":"Lucain made the cache-binding fix in Sept 2026 [assisted] with Claude Code.","basis":"21813188ba19","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"webhooks","name":"Webhooks server and payloads","kind":"module","summary":"Gradio/FastAPI-based webhook receiver and typed payload definitions.","decision":"Optional server built on Gradio/FastAPI with pydantic payloads.","alternatives":"Documented raw HTTP only.","why":"Easy local webhook handling in Spaces.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/_webhooks_server.py","src/huggingface_hub/_webhooks_payload.py"],"centrality":2,"clusters":["C5.1"],"scope":"architectural","history":[{"sha":"25e20ef","date":"2023-04-14","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"[Feat] Webhook server (#1410)"}],"importance":0.247,"orientation":{"purpose":"Lets a user run a small local server to receive Hub webhook events. It provides typed payload definitions for them.","decision":"An optional server built on Gradio and FastAPI, with pydantic payload models. Documenting raw HTTP only was not chosen. The reason given is easy webhook handling in Spaces.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_webhooks_server.py","what":"webhook server"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_webhooks_payload.py","what":"payload models"}],"shaped_by":"Lucain wrote it in April 2023 [human].","basis":"60dc8626e074","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}}]}$u6221422c$::jsonb,
    $u7d981bbd${"units":[{"id":"hf-api","name":"HfApi client","kind":"boundary","summary":"The monolithic HfApi class and module-level wrappers that expose nearly every Hub REST operation as the library's public API.","decision":"One giant HfApi class with a thin function-per-method facade re-exported through a statically generated lazy-import __init__, using dataclass return types.","alternatives":"Split per-resource clients (repos, spaces, collections); a generated OpenAPI client; pydantic models for responses.","why":"Backwards-compatible single entry point that downstream libraries already depend on; dataclasses replaced ReprMixin for lightweight typed results.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/hf_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/__init__.py","src/huggingface_hub/community.py","src/huggingface_hub/_space_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/_inference_endpoints.py","src/huggingface_hub/_jobs_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/endpoint_helpers.py","src/huggingface_hub/dataclasses.py"],"centrality":5,"scope":"architectural","importance":1.0,"history":[{"sha":"f590bdf","date":"2023-11-02","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Mario Šaško","subject":"Replace `ReprMixin` with dataclasses (#1788)"},{"sha":"0275ba9","date":"2022-12-08","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"Manage space hardware and secrets programmatically (#1243)"},{"sha":"aa4a792","date":"2023-07-26","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Freddy Boulton","subject":"Request Persistent Storage (#1571)"},{"sha":"ce00270","date":"2024-05-24","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Michael","subject":"[wip] Implement webhooks API (#2209)"},{"sha":"3bb08e2","date":"2026-10-01","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"Lucain","subject":"[Endpoints] Migrate catalog to the new /api/v1 API (#4928)"}],"parent":null,"orientation":{"purpose":"The main Python entry point for talking to the Hub's REST API: repos, files, discussions, Spaces, collections, webhooks and more. Other code and downstream libraries call it rather than making raw HTTP requests.","decision":"One large HfApi class, with module-level functions that forward to its methods and a generated lazy-import __init__. Per-resource clients, a generated OpenAPI client and pydantic responses were not chosen. The history points to backward compatibility for existing users, and dataclasses replaced ReprMixin for lightweight typed results.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/hf_api.py","what":"HfApi class and its result dataclasses"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/__init__.py","what":"public exports, auto-generated lazy imports"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_space_api.py","what":"Space runtime and hardware types"}],"shaped_by":"Several humans (Mario Šaško, Lucain, Freddy Boulton, Michael) shaped it from 2022 to 2024 [human]; Lucain's 2026 endpoints migration was [assisted].","basis":"56a4f54b5eb4","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"download-cache","name":"Download and cache layer","kind":"module","summary":"File and snapshot downloads with a git-like blob/snapshot cache, ETag resolution, Xet transfers, tree-listing cache and a cross-repo shared blob store.","decision":"Symlink-based content-addressed cache layout with degraded no-symlink fallback, local-dir metadata mode, and on-disk caching of tree listings and shared blobs.","alternatives":"Flat file cache; git clone; external cache service.","why":"Dedup of revisions and offline use; the layout is relied on by downstream libraries. Recent AI-assisted work added tree cache and shared blob store.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/file_download.py","src/huggingface_hub/_snapshot_download.py","src/huggingface_hub/_local_folder.py","src/huggingface_hub/_tree_cache.py","src/huggingface_hub/_revision.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_cache_manager.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_xet.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_xet_progress_reporting.py"],"centrality":5,"scope":"architectural","importance":0.751,"history":[{"sha":"f124f8b","date":"2022-05-25","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Julien Chaumond","subject":"New git-aware cache file layout (#801)"},{"sha":"6a4538b","date":"2022-10-13","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"[RFC] Proposal for a way to cache files in downstream libraries (#1088)"},{"sha":"8139641","date":"2026-06-29","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"Lucain","subject":"[Download] Cache repo tree listing on disk in snapshot_download (#4394)"},{"sha":"6e3d21f","date":"2026-09-17","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"célina","subject":"[Cache] Add cross-repo shared blob store (#4498)"}],"parent":null,"orientation":{"purpose":"Downloads single files or whole repos from the Hub and stores them in a local cache. Revisions are deduplicated, offline use works, and repeated downloads are cheap.","decision":"A git-like cache of content-addressed blobs with snapshot symlinks, a fallback for systems without symlinks, and a metadata mode for local directories. Later work added on-disk tree-listing caching and a cross-repo shared blob store. Flat caches, git clones and external services were not used. The layout is relied on by downstream libraries.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/file_download.py","what":"hf_hub_download, ETag resolution, cache layout"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_snapshot_download.py","what":"whole-repo download"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_tree_cache.py","what":"tree listing cache"}],"shaped_by":"Julien Chaumond and Lucain designed the layout in 2022 [human]; Lucain and célina added the tree cache and shared blob store in 2026 [assisted].","basis":"786df2ad347d","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"http-auth-config","name":"HTTP, auth and configuration core","kind":"decision","summary":"Shared httpx client factory with retry/backoff, header building, token resolution and env-driven constants used by all network code.","decision":"Centralized http_backoff helpers, build_hf_headers, multi-token local store with login/OAuth/OIDC flows, and all configuration via environment-variable constants in constants.py.","alternatives":"Per-module HTTP clients; keyring-only auth; config files.","why":"Uniform retry, error mapping and user-agent behavior; multi-token support and browser OAuth were added for user convenience.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/utils/_http.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_headers.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_auth.py","src/huggingface_hub/_login.py","src/huggingface_hub/_oauth.py","src/huggingface_hub/_oidc.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_oauth_device.py","src/huggingface_hub/constants.py","src/huggingface_hub/errors.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_validators.py"],"centrality":5,"scope":"architectural","importance":0.687,"history":[{"sha":"6fcc7b3","date":"2024-10-01","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Celina Hanouti","subject":"Support multiple tokens locally (#2549)"},{"sha":"d242977","date":"2026-06-16","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"célina","subject":"[Auth] Browser-based OAuth login  (#4354)"}],"parent":null,"orientation":{"purpose":"The shared foundation for network access: HTTP client creation with retries, request headers, token lookup, login flows, error types and environment-driven settings.","decision":"Retry helpers, header building and every configuration constant sit in one place, instead of each module having its own HTTP client. Auth supports multiple stored tokens and browser OAuth login. Keyring-only auth and config files were not chosen. The aim is uniform retry, error and user-agent behaviour, plus convenience.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/utils/_http.py","what":"client factory and backoff helpers"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_login.py","what":"login, logout and token storage"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/constants.py","what":"environment-variable constants"}],"shaped_by":"Celina Hanouti (2024) and célina (2026) wrote the multi-token and OAuth commits alone [human].","basis":"0b4a4c7af3ac","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"commit-upload","name":"Commit and upload pipeline","kind":"flow","summary":"Turns CommitOperation objects into Hub commits, handling LFS and Xet uploads, NDJSON streaming and multi-commit upload_folder.","decision":"Commits are streamed as NDJSON with pre-upload classification into regular/LFS/Xet, and large folders are uploaded through a streamed multi-commit pipeline powered by hf_xet.","alternatives":"Git-based pushes; one-shot multipart commit; separate large-folder API.","why":"Allows many files per commit and resumable large uploads; Xet gives chunk-level dedup. The pipeline was added by AI-assisted work and supersedes upload_large_folder.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/_commit_api.py","src/huggingface_hub/lfs.py","src/huggingface_hub/_upload_pipeline.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_lfs.py","src/huggingface_hub/_commit_scheduler.py","src/huggingface_hub/utils/_chunk_utils.py"],"centrality":4,"scope":"architectural","importance":0.524,"history":[{"sha":"7e089e6","date":"2022-10-21","klass":"human","agent":null,"author":"Lucain","subject":"Create commit by streaming a ndjson payload (allow lots of file in single commit) (#1117)"},{"sha":"97ea04b","date":"2026-06-16","klass":"assisted","agent":"claude-code","author":"Lucain","subject":"[Upload] Streamed multi-commit upload_folder powered by Xet (#4331)"}],"parent":null,"orientation":{"purpose":"Turns a list of add, delete and copy operations into a Hub commit. It decides how each file travels (plain, LFS or Xet) and handles large folder uploads.","decision":"Commits are sent as streamed NDJSON after files are classified as regular, LFS or Xet. Large folders go through a streamed multi-commit pipeline on hf_xet, which supersedes upload_large_folder. Git pushes, one-shot multipart commits and a separate large-folder API were not used. Xet is chosen for chunk-level dedup and resumability.","where":[{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_commit_api.py","what":"CommitOperation classes and commit logic"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/_upload_pipeline.py","what":"streamed multi-commit upload"},{"path":"src/huggingface_hub/lfs.py","what":"LFS batch upload"}],"shaped_by":"Lucain wrote the NDJSON streaming in 2022 [human] and the Xet multi-commit pipeline in 2026 [assisted].","basis":"dcab184bb304","head":"2c61ae8c11eedb1b79e262dd9eb5e68962cac063","generated_at":"2026-11-15T07:29:34+00:00"}},{"id":"cli","name":"hf CLI","kind":"boundary","summary":"Typer-based `hf` command line with groups per resource and a shared output/format layer.","decision":"Typer groups registered in hf.py, with a global `out` singleton supporting auto/json/human/quiet/agent formats, centralized error handling and generated reference docs.","alternatives":"argparse/click directly; separate scripts per command; plain print output.","why":"Consistent machine- and human-readable output (including agent use); CLAUDE.md prescribes the conventions. Much of it was built or migrated with AI assistance.","paths":["src/huggingface_hub/cli","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_cli_utils.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_output.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_errors.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_help_formatter.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_framework.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/hf.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/repos.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/models.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/datasets.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/spaces.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/buckets.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/cache.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/auth.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/upload.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/download.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/jobs.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/sandbox.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/extensions.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/skills.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_skills.py","src/huggingface_hub/cli/_uv_script_header.py"],"centrality":4,"scope":"architectural","